"""H2-2 cathode integration for C-1 (fo_h2_2_cathode_integration): deterministic builder.

Writes ``h2_2_cathode_integration_v1.json`` next to this file from the explicit, sourced inputs in ``INPUTS`` and the
evaluation grids in ``GRIDS``. Standard library only; nothing is imported from ``abep_sim`` (the test cross-checks the
relations shared with ``abep_sim/cathode_integration.py`` and the constants in ``abep_sim/constants.py``).

Rules this script follows (CLAUDE.md rules 3, 6, 10; docs/EVIDENCE.md):
  * every number used in a computation lives in ``INPUTS`` (with source, locator and evidence class) or in ``GRIDS``
    (explicit evaluation grids, labelled as such, never a design value or a device claim);
  * every relation takes its inputs as arguments; a missing, non-finite or out-of-range input raises
    ``H22InputError``; nothing falls back to a default;
  * no Hall transport closure, no screening candidate, no superseded 0-D Hall number and no withdrawn v1.2-v1.6 number
    is used; no thrust, efficiency, discharge current or plasma state is predicted;
  * PENDING values name the parallel lane path that owns them; nothing here imports or reads those lanes.

Usage::

    python docs/hardware/h2/h2_2_cathode_integration/build_h2_2_cathode_integration.py            # write the JSON
    python docs/hardware/h2/h2_2_cathode_integration/build_h2_2_cathode_integration.py --check    # byte-compare
    python docs/hardware/h2/h2_2_cathode_integration/build_h2_2_cathode_integration.py --verify-pins
"""
